{"id":"chatcmpl-c5eb6ce3-70db-49e6-9fdb-f54d240a0c94","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248797,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach to medical image interpretation: rather than trusting a single model's output, the agent cross-checks findings using multiple independent tools (expert reasoning, grounded reporting, and phrase localization). The key insight is that laterality and localization errors are common, so confirming spatial grounding against the image is essential before committing to an answer. The pattern generalizes to any visual question-answering task where distinguishing between similar options (e.g., left vs. right) requires spatial verification.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Cross-validate a primary diagnostic claim with at least one independent localization/grounding tool before answering, especially when options differ only by spatial attribute (side, region, position).\",\n    \"When options are near-symmetric (left vs. right, upper vs. lower), explicitly request laterality/localization confirmation rather than relying on descriptive text alone.\",\n    \"Use a domain-expert reasoning tool first to generate a hypothesis, then use grounding tools to verify the hypothesis against the actual image evidence.\",\n    \"Anchor the final answer to concrete spatial evidence (e.g., 'localized to patient's right lung base, image left') to guard against left/right confusion in radiological images.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Always confirm laterality with a grounding/localization tool; radiological left/right is viewer-inverted, so state the mapping explicitly. Use expert reasoning to form a hypothesis, then verify with independent tools.\",\n    \"Visual multiple-choice with spatial distractors\": \"When answer options differ only by location/side, prioritize tools that return coordinates or bounding regions over descriptive text tools. Treat descriptive agreement as weak evidence.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification workflows\": \"Sequence tools from hypothesis-generating (expert reasoning) to hypothesis-testing (grounding/localization). Only answer after at least one independent confirmation of the discriminating attribute.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the discriminating attribute (side/region) is independently verified by a localization tool, not just described in text.\",\n    \"Check that the final answer's spatial claim matches the image orientation (patient left vs. image left) before submitting.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":504,"total_tokens":963,"completion_tokens":459,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":504},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":459}}}